 "text": "One of the first implantable pacemakers started with the wrong part. 1950s, Buffalo, New York. Engineer Wilson Greatbatch is building a device to record heartbeats. He installs the wrong part by mistake. Instead of recording, the circuit starts to pulse, steady, like a heartbeat. He realizes this could keep a weak heart beating. With surgeon William Chardack, he builds a tiny pacemaker that fits inside the body. In 1960, their pacemaker is implanted in a patient. Every legend has a beginning.",
